# Governance JSON artifacts: canonical LF in git and on Linux CI (manifest SHA256 pins).
governance/artifacts/*.json text eol=lf
# Harness-owned config (RC-382): the Claude Code harness rewrites .claude/*.json with
# platform terminators whenever it persists settings. MEASURED 2026-08-15: settings.json
# was committed LF, flipped to CRLF, restored to LF by hand, and flipped BACK within a
# minute - a file an external tool owns cannot be held to a terminator by hand-restoring
# it, and the churn left the worktree permanently dirty, which in turn made the Stop
# supervisor's worktree-identity check fail an otherwise-clean turn. Pinning eol=lf gives
# git ownership: the blob stays LF no matter what the harness writes to disk.
.claude/*.json text eol=lf
# Model artifacts (ML-PIPE Item 4): byte-exact round-trip is mandatory - the
# bundle integrity manifests and the drift-recovery record pin EXACT bytes,
# so git must never EOL-normalize anything under models/ (the CRLF smudge on
# tracked *_meta.json was the GIT_EOL evidence complication AND left the
# canonical worktree permanently dirty after the TSLA disposition merge).
models/** -text
